### 🌐 Language Filter — What Was Added

**A prominent filter bar** has been injected directly below the page title, styled with Twitch's purple brand colours. It contains:

| Element | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **Dropdown selector** | Lists every language tag detected on the page, plus a "Show All Languages" default. Your last selection is remembered in `localStorage` and restored on the next visit. |
| **Status badge** | Shows a live count like `14 hidden · 6 shown` when a filter is active — disappears when all streams are shown. |
| **Help text** | A subtle reminder that only streams *with* the selected language tag are visible. |

**How filtering works:**
- Each stream card has Twitch language tags (e.g. `English`, `Español`, `Deutsch`) stored as `<a aria-label="Tag, English">`.
- When you pick a language, every card **without** a matching tag is immediately hidden.
- The rule re-runs automatically as new stream cards load (infinite scroll), so newly-loaded cards are filtered too.
- Selecting **"Show All Languages"** instantly restores all cards.

